WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.564
If you have used VLOOKUP in Excel, you will love Merge.

2
00:00:04.564 --> 00:00:09.356
In this lesson, you will learn to join two tables on a matching column,

3
00:00:09.356 --> 00:00:14.831
choose the right join kind, and expand the result to bring in the columns you need.

4
00:00:14.831 --> 00:00:16.200
Let's connect our tables!

5
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.501
We have two queries.

6
00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:24.757
The main Financial Sample table, and a smaller one with only Segment and Total Sale.

7
00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:28.260
We want to bring Total Sale into the main table.

8
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.123
On the Home tab, open Combine and choose Merge Queries.

9
00:01:03.123 --> 00:01:05.942
The window shows the first table on top.

10
00:01:05.942 --> 00:01:08.760
In the list, I choose the second table.

11
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.521
Now click the matching column in both tables.

12
00:01:32.521 --> 00:01:33.982
Here it is Segment.

13
00:01:33.982 --> 00:01:39.460
Power BI warns you until both tables have a selected column of the same type.

14
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.820
The Join Kind is Left Outer:

15
00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.260
all rows from the first table, and matching rows from the second.

16
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.330
At the bottom, Power BI tells you how many rows match.

17
00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:01.660
Here, seven hundred of seven hundred. A perfect match!

18
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:02.762
Click OK.

19
00:02:02.762 --> 00:02:05.921
A new column appears, and each cell says Table.

20
00:02:05.921 --> 00:02:09.080
That is the matched data, waiting to be opened.

21
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:15.034
Click the expand icon on the column header, tick the columns you want, here

22
00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:20.080
Total Sale, and untick Use original column name as prefix. Then click OK.

23
00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.803
Now Total Sale sits inside our main table, row by row.

24
00:02:26.803 --> 00:02:29.860
One merge replaced a lot of manual lookups!

25
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.191
Finally, Close and Apply loads every query into the report.

26
00:03:03.191 --> 00:03:07.860
Merge is one of the most powerful tools you have. Use it well!

